<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="bb4bf44c">The report mock-up design process begins during requirement gathering and requires inputs from all System Development Life
Cycle (SDLC) teams (analysis, development, and testing teams) along with expertise from various systems owners (business
and technical).</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="267cc658"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="bc9e95d9">&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Report mock-ups are mostly used for internal reporting or when new reports are being developed.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        For the development of regulatory and compliance reports, mock-ups might not be required as the&lt;br /&gt;
        structures for these reports are mostly finalized and dictated by regulatory agencies.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        The reporting platform and user interface should be taken into account while designing mock-ups and any platform
        constraints should also be taken into account.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="4caf726f"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="f31e1d9d">&lt;p&gt;
    The purpose of this task is:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        To provide stakeholders with an opportunity to validate the technical team&apos;s understanding of the underlying
        requirements before the reports are developed.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        To identify various display parameters that can be used to present reporting data and select the most appropriate
        format.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        To present options for drill down capabilities and hierarchical displays within the report, which will act as tools
        for better decision making by the stakeholders.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
